{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99b9c3842e40e4102ae86b3317f26103c80cdb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2021$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> can be rearranged to form other four-digit whole numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80c1201505153e784f51e62ccf23513810de7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. What is the largest possible difference between two such four-digit whole numbers?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246d3de7fbadc80045129ba64a11ae3b9f8fed66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1188 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1098 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 1080 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2088 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To maximise the difference between the two four-digit numbers, we can make one number as large as possible and the other number as small as possible.\n</p><p>We can list all such four-digit numbers, which is simple to do because there aren't that many:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d19f6c66057ecac4ed06919ad4718379419937d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1022$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/2/1826f8b508ab5d227883815290456efc840ca618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1202$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d8430876eec5686b4221bfe5d47e7fd9eafd656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1220$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f48f95ec89b6c50220ecbbbb6130586135db8ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99b9c3842e40e4102ae86b3317f26103c80cdb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2021$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c5b9b02e89f9c33e1d23bad8d7bfa6a0d466e5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2102$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/100ebc2d25fad25eacb2270ab28a5bc8aa0e89b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91e3ab886c915913ffc639c8e39fd02d5d6d45e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2201$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a37a22df4e5ed37e38ebd8c6e5b214685fc68c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d19f6c66057ecac4ed06919ad4718379419937d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1022$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is the lowest number and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a37a22df4e5ed37e38ebd8c6e5b214685fc68c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is the largest number here. The difference between the two is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76bc4e8039dc5884911bd0c4ca6ff57217fce103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2210 - 1022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/955feff6130ef41dc0cfa58dfb24101ac2ab749a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 1188}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"85\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rather than listing all of the possible values, we can realise that the largest such four-digit number would have the largest digits as the thousands, then the hundreds, and then the tens place while the smallest such four-digit number would minimise the thousands, hundreds, and tens digit.\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a37a22df4e5ed37e38ebd8c6e5b214685fc68c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> would be the largest number and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d19f6c66057ecac4ed06919ad4718379419937d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1022$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> would be the lowest number. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cannot go in the thousands place because the number would be a three-digit number, rather than a four-digit number.\n</p><p>Like in solution 1, this ends up in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/955feff6130ef41dc0cfa58dfb24101ac2ab749a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 1188}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"85\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Proble